# Archie Lillingston - Character File
# Lonesome Trail (Working Title)
# Created: February 17, 2026
# Author: Dale Salvador

character:
  name: Archie Lillingston
  aliases:
    - Archibald Lillingston
    - "The Quiet Broker"
  role: Central Quest Giver / Merchant / Arms Dealer
  occupation:
    - Bartender (primary public role)
    - Arms Dealer (secondary hidden role)
  family:
    status: Wealthy, influential in Bunco City alcohol industry
    history: Family controls supply and distribution across Bunco and nearby towns; lineage emphasizes power and control.
  personality:
    traits:
      - Calm
      - Rarely reactive
      - Patient
      - Calculating
      - Observant
      - Adaptive
    demeanor: Speaks in neutral, business-like tones; avoids emotional displays; evaluates people and situations for utility.
    philosophy: Control is everything; whether through peace or violence, Archie ensures he maintains influence.
  narrative_role:
    overview: |
      Central figure in Bunco City. All major quests pass through him. He adapts his offers to the player's moral path:
        - Rider (violent) path: Offers secondary “arms dealing” shop, violent expansion quests.
        - Domestic (peaceful) path: Provides bar job, safer quests, no access to weapons or expansion.
      Archie manipulates indirectly. He is never an overt antagonist but a constant facilitator of the player's ambitions.
    influence:
      - Player autonomy: He adapts to choices but ensures the player remains within his system.
      - World-building: His family wealth and control shape Bunco City’s economy and social structure.
      - Moral tension: He embodies the consequences of power without judgment; his calm neutrality emphasizes the player’s internal conflict.
  quest_mechanics:
    rider_path:
      - Name: "Expansion Contract"
        Description: Player is tasked with eliminating obstacles to establish a new bar in a rival town.
        Reward: Access to weapons, resources, and the "Second Shop."
        Conditions: Player actively pursues violence and outlaw status.
    domestic_path:
      - Name: "Bar Assistant"
        Description: Player helps in the bar, manages supplies, and builds local relationships.
        Reward: Safe income, minor story influence, no access to weapons.
        Conditions: Player chooses domestic/love-oriented path.
    second_shop:
      Description: Unlockable only on Rider path; arms dealer network activated. Player can purchase weapons, explosives, and specialized gear.
      Location: Hidden area behind the bar.
      Tone: Cold, business-like. No morality discussed. Archie evaluates usefulness only.
  appearance:
    description: |
      Well-dressed but unassuming. Always composed, rarely showing emotion. Bar is tidy, almost immaculate, reflecting his personality.
    typical_clothing:
      - Waistcoat
      - Shirt with rolled sleeves
      - Sturdy boots
      - Minimal accessories
  relationships:
    player:
      - Type: Manipulative facilitator
      - Notes: Adapts offers and quests to align with player choices; always maintains calm neutrality.
    girl_character:
      - Type: Observant
      - Notes: Senses his control instinctively; cautious of his influence.
    Father Rufus Mutz:
      - Type: Indirect ally/contrast
      - Notes: Archie interacts for influence but avoids moral conflict; respects Father Rufus’ authority when beneficial.
    Sheriff George Storen:
      - Type: Strategic relationship
      - Notes: Bribes or influences when necessary; removes obstacles to expand his bar/alcohol influence.
  dialogue_style:
    tone: Neutral, measured, business-oriented
    examples:
      - "There's a man blocking opportunity. I’d appreciate it if that obstacle were removed."
      - "Your path seems set. I can assist accordingly."
      - "Whether you choose peace or chaos, Bunco has room for you. Just know I always see the bigger picture."
  notes:
    - Archie never overtly judges morality; he reacts only to usefulness.
    - Player perception of him changes based on choices, but his behavior remains constant.
    - Optional lore hints can be included in the bar’s decor and ledgers, showing his long-term planning and empire-building.

